2 0 obj
<<
/Producer (PyPDF2)
/Title (Systems\040of\040land\040registration\040aspects\040and\040effects)
/Author (Jaap\040Zevenbergen)
/Subject (concepts\040Land\040as\040the\040object\040of\040property\040rights\040is\040different\040from\040most\040other\040types\040of\040property\056\040In\040many\040cases\040there\040is\040not\040a\040\217logical\220\040object\056\040The\040object\040has\040to\040be\040defined\054\040has\040to\040be\040legally\040constructed\054\040and\040can\040change\040relatively\040easily\040\050compare\040\247\0402\0562\0565\040and\040\247\0403\0562\0564\051\056\040The\040objects\040are\040separated\040by\040boundaries\040which\040define\040where\040one\040landowner\220s\040territory\040ends\040and\040the\040next\040begins\056\040Even\040though\040there\040often\040is\040a\040reasonably\040high\040congruity\040between\040topographic\040boundary\040features\040and\040legal\040extent\054\040there\040is\040no\040necessary\040identity\040between\040the\040topography\040of\040a\040parcel\040and\040the\040legal\040extent\040of\040that\040parcel\056\040The\040extent\040and\040boundaries\040of\040land\040parcels\040are\040a\040matter\040of\040legal\040definition\056\040\050Burdon\0401998\072\040152\051\040Parcels\040and\040boundaries\040are\040abstract\040concepts\056\040This\040makes\040a\040very\040large\040difference\040with\040most\040other\040types\040of\040geo\055information\054\040which\040depicts\040\217real\040life\220\040geographical\040phenomenon\056\040\050compare\040van\040der\040Molen\0402001\072\04015\051\056\040Title\040plans\040and\040parcel\040maps\040are\040legal\040documents\040in\040a\040graphical\040form\040and\040not\040just\040another\040dataset\040for\040a\040geographical\040information\040system\040\050GIS\051\040\050Burdon\0401998\072\040154\051\056\040Similarly\040the\040rights\040in\040land\040are\040abstract\040concepts\056\040Property\040rights\040are\040an\040important\040example\040of\040institutions\073\040humanly\040devised\040constraints\040that\040shape\040human\040interactions\040\050see\040\247\0401\0562\0563\051\056\040Rights\040in\040land\040are\040usually\040described\040in\040a\040complex\040system\040of\040land\040tenure\056\040Through\040the\040abstract\040concept\054\040land\040rights\040can\040grow\040into\040much\040more\040than\040a\040distribution\040mechanism\040for\040land\040use\056\040The\040rights\040can\040be\040activated\040as\040capital\054\040allowing\040inter\040alia\040for\040\050cheaper\051\040loans\040against\040collateral\040\050see\040\247\0401\0562\0561\051\056\04078\040SYSTEMS\040OF\040LAND\040REGISTRATION)
/Keywords (11\040Nov\0402002\054\040Land\040registration\054\040Land\040tenure\054\040Property\040rights\054\040Boundary\040\050real\040estate\051\054\040Land\040use)
>>
endobj
